# Fix User Model and Authentication

This plan addresses the critical and medium severity issues identified in the review of the `User` model.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The authentication field will change from `username` to `email`. This is a breaking change for any existing login logic or test users.
> The `is_academico` boolean field is being replaced by a `role` choice field.

## Proposed Changes

### accounts app

#### [MODIFY] [models.py](file:///d:/Repositorios/AllocGest-DESUP/project_root/apps/accounts/models.py)
- Implement `UserManager` to support email-based authentication.
- Update `User` model:
    - Set `email` as `unique=True`.
    - Set `USERNAME_FIELD = 'email'`.
    - Set `REQUIRED_FIELDS = ['username', 'cpf']`.
    - Replace `is_academico` with `role` (using `TextChoices`).
    - Update `ordering` to use `email`.
    - Update `__str__` to use `email`.

#### [MODIFY] [admin.py](file:///d:/Repositorios/AllocGest-DESUP/project_root/apps/accounts/admin.py)
- Fix user import (use `from .models import User` instead of `django.contrib.auth.models`).
- Update `list_display` to reflect the changes (e.g., use `role` instead of `is_academico` if applicable, although it wasn't there before).

#### [MODIFY] [views.py](file:///d:/Repositorios/AllocGest-DESUP/project_root/apps/accounts/views.py)
- Fix user import.
- Simplify `login_view` logic since `authenticate` will now work with email directly.


## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `python manage.py makemigrations` and `python manage.py migrate`.
- Create a test script to:
    - Create a user with email and password.
    - Verify that authentication works using email.
    - Verify that creating a user with a duplicate email fails.
    - Verify that the `role` field works as expected.

### Manual Verification
- Test `createsuperuser` command to ensure it asks for `email` and `cpf`.
